{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined","id":988611,"title":"Curse of Lycaon examined.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-10-16T19:42:03-07:00","id":988611,"title":"Curse of Lycaon examined.","content":"it says simply it transforms a normal &quot;Human or animal, into a normal wolf&quot; <br /> <br /> a few follow up questions.<br /> <br /> is the destruction of their psyche complete or could it be some vestige lingers, for a while at least horrified, and fighting on hoping, in vain for a cure.<br /> <br /> Is it safe to say the &quot;Or animals&quot; edit in W20 was thinking dogs in particular?<br /> <br /> though I SERIOUSLY doubt Talons would view that as a curse, in any shape or form.<br /> <br /> indeed the miracle of reversing domestication, might have been how the gift originated.<br /> <br /> Do you think the Talons would be willing to help the new wolf, even if they'd once been an enemy, by &quot;inviting&quot; them into their pack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T19:52:30-07:00","id":988625,"title":"","content":"Whether any kind of psyche lingers depends on the ST. I think once the person is a wolf in thought, they'd treat the wolf just like any other wolf (at least after a time). The person has &quot;atoned&quot; for whatever crimes they did as a human. Initially though, the Red Talons might allow some kind of poetic justice such as human hunters killing the new wolf for predation done on livestock and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T20:58:46-07:00","id":988670,"title":"","content":"More importantly; if all it costs is *One* Measley Point of Gnosis to turn *any* Animal into a Wolf *forever*, what's stopping Red Talon Elders from using this Gift to go around and Replenish The Wolf Population? <br /> <br /> 9 wolves a day, followed by intense meditation, repeat the next day, that's 63 wolves a week.<br /> <br /> Multiply that by the 52 weeks a year, and you'll have 3276 *fertile* wolves, Per-Elder-Hero who *diligently* uses This Gift.<br /> <br /> Multiply That By another TEN years, 32,760 wolves made per elder is nothing to be sneezed at.<br /> <br /> Who will in turn repopulate Garou Kinfolk Numbers, to say nothing of eventually increasing Garou numbers.<br /> <br /> The mere existence of this gift, not to mention the sheer *ease* of its use, makes the alleged &quot;perilous&quot; situation of The Red Talon Tribe patently ridiculous when you think about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-16T21:14:22-07:00","id":988680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=988670#post988670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly; if all it costs is *One* Measley Point of Gnosis to turn *any* Animal into a Wolf *forever*, what's stopping Red Talon Elders from using this Gift to go around and Replenish The Wolf Population?<br /> <br /> 9 wolves a day, followed by intense meditation, repeat the next day, that's 63 wolves a week.<br /> <br /> Multiply that by the 52 weeks a year, and you'll have 3276 *fertile* wolves, Per-Elder-Hero who *diligently* uses This Gift.<br /> <br /> Multiply That By another TEN years, 32,760 wolves made per elder is nothing to be sneezed at.<br /> <br /> Who will in turn repopulate Garou Kinfolk Numbers, to say nothing of eventually increasing Garou numbers.<br /> <br /> The mere existence of this gift, not to mention the sheer *ease* of its use, makes the alleged &quot;perilous&quot; situation of The Red Talon Tribe patently ridiculous when you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think your grossly Underestimating the difficulty in replenishing gnosis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T08:37:41-07:00","id":988877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=988680#post988680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think your grossly Underestimating the difficulty in replenishing gnosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's that, and how the Garou are kind of constantly in a state of war and often don't get the free time to do this.<br /> <br /> However, it does bring up an interesting point about what happens when they do get those moments. People just suddenly up and disappear, with no human traces and no evidence of foul play. Do people just forget after a while?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:17:20-07:00","id":988888,"title":"","content":"You CAN in *theory*, create fertile wolves that you can breed Wolf Kinfolk with, right? (As far as I understand, the equation seems to be &quot;Garou X Normal Human/Wolf = Kinfolk offspring&quot;), right?<br /> <br /> Because if the answer is affirmative? This Fifth Level Gift is one potentially *potent* Secret-Weapon in tipping the balance of The War by creating more Spiritually (Gnosis) potent Lupus Warriors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> *Literally* out of The Birds and The Bees if you are starved for immediate recruits and &quot;volunteers&quot; (The Gift *did&quot; say ANY Animal, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4684,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","user":"Lin Liren","date":". 10-17-2016, 12:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4684-lin-liren","name":"Lin Liren","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T09:53:01-07:00","id":988902,"title":"","content":"was wondering, how willing do you think talons would be to teach the gift to an elder of another tribe?<br /> <br /> as it their anything it could be used for they'd not approve of?<br /> <br /> the CoG gift &quot;Mercy&quot; could be used by a shadow Lord Judge of Doom to capture quary alive, making the gifts name seem extremely ironic.<br /> <br /> anything Curse of lycanon could be used for the talons wouldnt approve of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T10:16:46-07:00","id":988912,"title":"","content":"Tribal Gifts at the elder level are unlikely to end up shared.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=988888#post988888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You CAN in *theory*, create fertile wolves that you can breed Wolf Kinfolk with, right? (As far as I understand, the equation seems to be &quot;Garou X Normal Human/Wolf = Kinfolk offspring&quot;), right?<br /> <br /> Because if the answer is affirmative? This Fifth Level Gift is one potentially *potent* Secret-Weapon in tipping the balance of The War by creating more Spiritually (Gnosis) potent Lupus Warriors. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> *Literally* out of The Birds and The Bees if you are starved for immediate recruits and &quot;volunteers&quot; (The Gift *did&quot; say ANY Animal, after all. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )</div> </div> </div> </div>Those factors are a non-question; we already know how it works. The interesting question is how the world reacts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T11:11:01-07:00","id":988937,"title":"","content":"Wolves need teritory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:08:18-07:00","id":989135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=988670#post988670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More importantly; if all it costs is *One* Measley Point of Gnosis to turn *any* Animal into a Wolf *forever*, what's stopping Red Talon Elders from using this Gift to go around and Replenish The Wolf Population?</div> </div> </div> </div>While the book just says Gnosis, I've always held it is Permanent, not temporary Gnosis.<br /> <br /> As ST, I would also restrict it to only certain humans who violated some kind of sacred taboo, not just anyone.<br /> <br /> I didn't actually read close enough that the Gift affects animals too, not just people. I'd ignore that as well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:16:22-07:00","id":989138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=989135#post989135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the book just says Gnosis, I've always held it is Permanent, not temporary Gnosis.<br /> <br /> As ST, I would also restrict it to only certain humans who violated some kind of sacred taboo, not just anyone.<br /> <br /> I didn't actually read close enough that the Gift affects animals too, not just people. I'd ignore that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If it had been meant to be permanent Gnosis, the numerous revisions from first edition to now probably would have made it permanent. As-is, it's a temporary point, and that's what we have to work with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:33:52-07:00","id":989150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=989135#post989135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While the book just says Gnosis, I've always held it is Permanent, not temporary Gnosis.<br /> <br /> As ST, I would also restrict it to only certain humans who violated some kind of sacred taboo, not just anyone.<br /> <br /> I didn't actually read close enough that the Gift affects animals too, not just people. I'd ignore that as well.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Saur Ops Specialist is right<br /> <br /> The effecting animals not just people is a rewrite for W20<br /> <br /> id use it , but only for effecting DOGS<br /> <br /> especialy dogs who've done something to earn a Talons compassion, or gratitude<br /> <br /> such as helping his pack out.<br /> <br /> <br /> Allowing it to effect ANY animal, is just ludicrous.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Oh thoughts on what a pentex first team, group of DNA scientists, or SAD agents would think of seeing a coleague, subjected to it?<br /> <br /> or think themselves when subjected to it as they felt their psyche break down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T19:48:44-07:00","id":989160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lin Liren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=988670#post988670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Snip</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that there are probably only a handful of rank 5 Talons (I would say 5 or less), and they would certainly be too busy doing Elder stuff to dedicate their lives to this sort of thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/988611-curse-of-lycaon-examined?p=989150#post989150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The effecting animals not just people is a rewrite for W20<br /> <br /> id use it , but only for effecting DOGS<br /> <br /> especialy dogs who've done something to earn a Talons compassion, or gratitude<br /> <br /> such as helping his pack out.</div> </div> </div> </div>I rather like the idea of it being used to gift a dog with Wolfhood<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-17T20:20:39-07:00",